# Production API base for the Vite build.
#
# Deliberately EMPTY. nginx (deploy/aws/nginx.conf) serves this bundle and
# proxies `location /api/` to http://localhost:8000 on the same origin, so
# src/config.js resolving API_BASE to "" makes every call a same-origin
# /api/... request. That is what the working production bundle does.
#
# Do NOT put an absolute host here. Vite inlines this value at build time, so
# a wrong host is baked into the bundle and every API call fails. The previous
# value was a leftover Railway placeholder (https://your-railway-url.railway.app)
# from before the EC2 move; a build carrying it would have broken production.
VITE_API_URL=
